# Holybro X500 V2 in Lucky: physics and the stand-in AltHold controller (X500Flight.cs).
# Read when Play starts: edit, save, press Play again. Format: NAME value, # starts a comment.
#
# SIM_*  is the drone itself: change these to close the sim2real gap with logs of the real one.
# Everything else mirrors ArduCopter: the X500v2 frame file (Tools/Frame_params/Holybro-X500v2-bdshot.param)
# where it sets a value, ArduCopter defaults otherwise. Angles in degrees, speeds in m/s.

# --- Physics (mass and inertia come from the MuJoCo model: 1.36 kg with the 4S 3300 mAh pack)
SIM_THST_MAX    11.3     # N per motor at full command (2216 KV920 + 1045 on 4S: ~1.15 kgf)
SIM_THST_EXPO   0.65     # thrust curve: thrust = (1-e)*u + e*u^2 of the command above spin min
SIM_MOT_TAU     0.05     # s, motor/prop time constant
SIM_YAW_COEF    0.016    # m, rotor drag torque per newton of thrust (yaw authority)
SIM_DRAG_CDA    0.04     # m^2, body drag area (Cd*A): sets top speed at full lean
SIM_DRAG_LIN    0.15     # N per m/s, rotor drag (blade flapping/induced drag)
SIM_ARM_LEN     0.25     # m, centre to motor (500 mm wheelbase)

# --- Motors (ESC command fraction, as ArduPilot outputs)
MOT_SPIN_ARM    0.07
MOT_SPIN_MIN    0.09
MOT_SPIN_MAX    0.95

# --- Attitude (ATC_*), from the X500v2 frame file
ANGLE_MAX       30
ATC_INPUT_TC    0.15
ATC_ACC_Y_MAX   359.55   # deg/s^2
ATC_ANG_RLL_P   26.35878
ATC_ANG_PIT_P   21.2236
ATC_ANG_YAW_P   8.53887
ATC_RAT_RLL_P   0.1255951
ATC_RAT_RLL_I   0.1255951
ATC_RAT_RLL_D   0.004905871
ATC_RAT_PIT_P   0.1466683
ATC_RAT_PIT_I   0.1466683
ATC_RAT_PIT_D   0.005201788
ATC_RAT_YAW_P   1.204564
ATC_RAT_YAW_I   0.1204564
ATC_RAT_YAW_D   0.02224096
ATC_RAT_IMAX    0.5
ATC_RAT_FLTD    21       # Hz, D-term filter

# --- Altitude hold (PSC_D_*, PILOT_*)
PSC_D_POS_P     1.0
PSC_D_VEL_P     5.0
PILOT_SPD_UP    2.5
PILOT_SPD_DN    2.5
PILOT_ACC_Z     2.5      # m/s^2
PILOT_Y_RATE    202.5    # deg/s
THR_DZ          0.1      # deadband around mid stick, fraction of half travel

# --- Sticks (Mode 2). Lucky's axes: 0 left X, 1 left Y, 2 right X, 3 right Y; a minus flips it (stick up reads negative)
RC_THR          -1       # left stick up/down: climb/descend, centre holds altitude
RC_YAW          0        # left stick left/right
RC_PIT          -3       # right stick up/down: forward/back
RC_RLL          2        # right stick left/right
RC_DZ           0.05     # stick deadzone
# Arm: left stick down and right for 2 s. Disarm on the ground: left stick down and left for 2 s.
# V on the keyboard switches the controller and camera between the X500 and Dronstein.
